---
// src/pages/hollywood/swarm/index.astro · 0928 V2
// V2: hub copy replaced (The Signature in the Swarm 0928 V3) — four questions
// instead of three, "Two Lies, One Root" retired; five entries in film order.
// The Signature in the Swarm — the fly-god page under Studios & Genre.
//
// This is a genre hub, not a study: it names Baal-zebub, states the doctrinal
// test every entry is measured by, and lists the films. The entries live in
// src/data/hollywood.js on the `swarm` card; adding a film is a data edit plus
// its page, nothing here.
//
// Built in Astro rather than as static HTML under public/hollywood/films, where
// its Studios siblings still sit. That legacy sub-site carries its own <head>,
// its own breadcrumb and its own stylesheet, so those pages get no site header,
// no theme, no social card and no search indexing. New work goes on the stack.
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { swarm, swarmEntries } from '../../../data/hollywood.js';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Signature in the Swarm — Hollywood | Nazaryah"
  description={swarm.description}
>
<div class="craft-shell">
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">Studios &amp; Genre — Hollywood</p>
  <h1>The Signature in the Swarm</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">{swarm.tagline}</p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <h2>The Name</h2>
  <p>
    Ahaziah, king of Israel, was badly hurt and sent men to ask Baal-zebub, the god of
    Ekron, whether he would live. Baal-zebub means lord of the fly. Elijah met the
    messengers on the road with a question and a sentence — is there not a God in
    Israel, and the king will not come down off that bed (2 Kings 1:2-4). He did not
    build the fly-god a temple. He asked him one question. That was enough. The same
    name is the title of the prince of devils in the gospels (Matthew 12:24).
  </p>
  <p>
    So the fly belongs to a devil, and asking that devil about your own healing was a
    capital matter. That is the Book's position, stated twice, in both testaments.
  </p>

  <h2>Why Hollywood Reaches For It</h2>
  <p>Flies gather where something has died. They do not cause the death. They announce it.</p>
  <p>
    That is what makes the swarm so useful to a storyteller. A cloud of insects tells an
    audience that something is deeply wrong here, and it says nothing at all about what
    law was broken, who broke it, or what it will cost to settle.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is the feeling of guilt with the courtroom stripped out. And it carries a devil's
    name the audience is never told.
  </p>

  <h2>The Doctrine Underneath</h2>
  <p>Every film on this page turns on one question. Where does evil live?</p>
  <p>
    Scripture answers plainly. Sin is the transgression of the law (1 John 3:4). A
    broken command. A charge on a record. It is not a substance in the flesh, not a
    residue in the meat, not an atmosphere a sensitive person can feel in a room.
  </p>
  <p>
    If sin is a substance, it comes out by technique — a gifted man, a ritual, a
    transfer. No law, no court, no judge. That is sorcery.
  </p>
  <p>
    If sin is a charge, it comes out by verdict — a standard, a witness, a sentence,
    and blood (Hebrews 9:22). That is Scripture.
  </p>
  <p>Every swarm below is arguing for the first one.</p>

  <h2>How to Read the Entries</h2>
  <p>Each film gets the same four questions.</p>
  <ol class="tests">
    <li>What does the fly actually do on screen?</li>
    <li>What is the fly being used to teach?</li>
    <li>What does the name behind it belong to?</li>
    <li>What does Scripture say instead?</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="close">
    The five are not connected by genre, studio, or decade. They are connected by an
    insect, and the insect has a name.
  </p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <h2 class="entries-head">The Entries</h2>
  <ul class="entries" role="list">
    {swarmEntries.map((e) => (
      <li class={`entry ${e.status}`}>
        <a href={e.href} class={`entry-link ${e.status === 'live' ? '' : 'is-coming'}`}>
          <span class="entry-n">{String(e.n).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <span class="entry-body">
            <span class="entry-title">{e.title}</span>
            <span class="entry-work">{e.work}</span>
            <span class="entry-tag">{e.tagline}</span>
            <span class="entry-verses">{e.verses}</span>
          </span>
          {e.status === 'live'
            ? <span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            : <span class="entry-soon">In production</span>}
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <p class="back-wrap"><a class="back" href="/hollywood">← Back to Hollywood</a></p>

  <hr class="rule" />
  <footer class="craft-footer">nazaryah.com</footer>
</main>
</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* The Hollywood house theme, scoped to this shell so it never leaks to the
     global header/footer. Same palette as The Craft and The Stars. */
  .craft-shell {
    --bg: #160a0c;
    --bg-raise: #201114;
    --ink: #ece1cd;
    --ink-soft: #b6a58f;
    --parchment: #ecd8a6;
    --gold: #c99a44;
    --gold-soft: #a98a53;
    --rule: rgba(201, 154, 68, 0.22);
    --display: "Cormorant Garamond", Georgia, serif;
    --body: "EB Garamond", Georgia, serif;
    --maxw: 46rem;

    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 80% at 50% -10%, #241318 0%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) 55%),
      radial-gradient(140% 120% at 50% 0%, #1d1012 0%, var(--bg) 60%);
    background-color: var(--bg);
    min-height: 80vh;
  }

  .wrap {
    max-width: var(--maxw);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) 1.4rem 4rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--body);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.32em;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .eyebrow::before,
  .eyebrow::after { content: "—"; color: var(--gold-soft); margin: 0 0.7em; }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--parchment);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: 0.015em;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 1.3rem + 3.4vw, 3.5rem);
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .subtitle {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1rem + 0.5vw, 1.3rem);
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-align: center;
  }

  hr.rule { border: 0; height: 1px; background: var(--rule); margin: 3rem auto; max-width: 20rem; }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0.9rem;
  }
  p { line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }

  blockquote {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 0.2rem 0 0.2rem 1.2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold-soft);
  }
  blockquote p { font-style: italic; color: var(--parchment); margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  blockquote cite {
    font-style: normal;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--gold-soft);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .tests { margin: 0 0 1.2rem; padding-left: 1.3rem; }
  .tests li { line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .tests li::marker { color: var(--gold-soft); }

  .close { font-style: italic; color: var(--parchment); }

  .entries-head { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1.6rem; }
  .entries { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .entry { margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .entry-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 3px;
    transition: border-color 0.2s, background 0.2s;
  }
  .entry-link:hover, .entry-link:focus-visible { border-color: var(--gold); outline: none; }
  .entry-link.is-coming { opacity: 0.6; }

  .entry-n {
    font-family: var(--display);
    color: var(--gold-soft);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  .entry-body { flex: 1; }
  .entry-title {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--parchment);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .entry-work { display: block; color: var(--gold-soft); font-size: 0.86rem; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
  .entry-tag { display: block; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-top: 0.4rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .entry-verses {
    display: block;
    color: var(--gold-soft);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }
  .entry-arrow { color: var(--gold); font-size: 1.1rem; padding-top: 0.15rem; }
  .entry-soon {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--gold-soft);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  .back-wrap { text-align: center; margin-top: 2.6rem; }
  .back {
    color: var(--gold);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }
  .back:hover { color: var(--parchment); }
  .back:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--gold); outline-offset: 3px; }

  .craft-footer {
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .entry-link { flex-wrap: wrap; }
  }
</style>
